issue.body:
If I write:

```
$ eslint Gruntfile.js app
```

I get no errors while if I execute:

```
$ eslint app
```

I get a lot of errors. `.eslintrc` for `Gruntfile.js` is defined in the same directory while `.eslintrc` for `app` - at `app/.eslintrc`.

The issue appears not only when used via a binary. I stumbled upon this issue via [grunt-eslint](https://github.com/sindresorhus/grunt-eslint), my config is as follows:

``` js
grunt.initConfig({
    eslint: {
        all: {
            src: [
                'Gruntfile.js',
                '{karma,protractor}*.conf.js',
                'app',
                'test',
                'grunt',
            ],
        },
    },
});
```
